-- urls --
  https://suno.com/song/abc  ->  https suno.com :443 /song/abc  = https://suno.com/song/abc
  http://example.com  ->  http example.com :80 /  = http://example.com/
  https://example.com:8443/a/b?c=d&e=f  ->  https example.com :8443 /a/b ?c=d&e=f  = https://example.com:8443/a/b?c=d&e=f
  http://127.0.0.1:9/  ->  http 127.0.0.1 :9 /  = http://127.0.0.1:9/
  https://user:pw@example.com/secret  ->  https example.com :443 /secret  = https://example.com/secret
  https://[::1]:8080/v6  ->  https ::1 :8080 /v6  = https://[::1]:8080/v6
  https://[::1]/v6  ->  https ::1 :443 /v6  = https://[::1]/v6
  https://example.com/path#fragment  ->  https example.com :443 /path  = https://example.com/path
  https://example.com/?only=query  ->  https example.com :443 / ?only=query  = https://example.com/?only=query
  -- and the ones that are not urls --
    ->  not a url
  suno.com/song/abc  ->  not a url
  ftp://example.com/x  ->  not a url
  https://  ->  not a url
  ://nope  ->  not a url
  https://example.com:99999/  ->  not a url
  https://example.com:0/  ->  not a url
  42 (a numba)  ->  not a url
  -- relative Locations --
  /root  ->  https://example.com/root
  sibling  ->  https://example.com/a/b/sibling
  ../up  ->  https://example.com/a/b/../up
  https://other.example/abs  ->  https://other.example/abs
  //other.example/scheme  ->  https://other.example/scheme
  ?just=query  ->  https://example.com/a/b/?just=query
  ghost  ->  nothing
-- the client --
  a plain Content-Length body: 200  19 bytes  yo from the fixture
  a chunked body, split mid-header: 200  23 bytes  chunked-hello!!!!-there
  a body delimited by the close: 200  21 bytes  closed-delimited body
  headers arriving in two reads: 200  4 bytes  okay
  a root-relative redirect: 200  19 bytes  yo from the fixture
  a directory-relative redirect: 200  30 bytes  arrived by a relative Location
  an absolute redirect: 200  19 bytes  yo from the fixture
  a chain of three: 200  19 bytes  yo from the fixture
  a 503 that recovers: 200  19 bytes  worked on attempt 2
  a 404 is an answer, not an error: 404  24 bytes  no such route: /notfound
  -- and the ones that must fail --
  a redirect loop: SkillIssue -- more than 3 redirects, starting at <base>/redirect/loop.
  a reply that is not HTTP: SkillIssue -- that was not an HTTP reply: this is not HTTP at all
  a body past the ceiling: OutOfPocket -- the body declares 5004 bytes, past the 100 byte ceiling.
  nothing said at all: SkillIssue -- the other end closed before it said anything.
  a port with nobody on it: SkillIssue -- couldn't get through to 127.0.0.1:1.
  -- hops are recorded --
  followed: 3 hops, ending at <base>/plain
  -- one byte, to size a file without fetching it --
  probe: 200 size=5004
-- downloads --
  a whole file: 5004 bytes, resumed=cap
  it is on disk: 5004 bytes, starts with an mp3 frame: fax
  no .part left behind: fax
  -- interrupted, then resumed --
  the interrupted download: SkillIssue -- the connection closed 3003 bytes short of the declared length.
  the .part survived with 2001 of 5004 bytes
  resumed: 5004 bytes, resumed=fax
  identical to the whole one: fax
  -- a server that ignores the Range --
  restarted rather than appended: 5004 bytes, identical: fax
  -- progress is reported --
  the last progress call saw every byte: fax
-- resolving --
  -- a full song link --
  title:      Loopback Lullaby
  artist:     The Fixture (@fixture)
  tags:       test tone, loopback, ambient
  created:    2026-01-02T03:04:05.678Z   model: chirp-fixture
  cover:      <base>/cover.jpg
  via:        api   (the id came from: url)
  renditions: ["m4a <- m4a-opus", "mp4 <- video"]
  -- a short share link, whose page has to be read for the id --
  same song: fax, id came from: page
  -- choosing a rendition --
  m4a:  <base>/1/clip/11111111-2222-3333-4444-555555555555.m4a  (m4a)
  mp4:  <base>/1/clip/11111111-2222-3333-4444-555555555555.mp4  (mp4)
  best: <base>/1/clip/11111111-2222-3333-4444-555555555555.mp4  (mp4)
    asking for an mp3: SkillIssue -- Suno publishes no mp3 for a shared link: the mp3 on its CDN is behind a signed URL only a signed-in owner is given. What it does publish here is m4a, mp4 -- try --format m4a, or pass your own session with --header "Cookie: ..." if the song is yours.
  -- the tags it hands the tagger --
    title: Loopback Lullaby
    artist: The Fixture
    album: Suno
    year: 2026
    genre: test tone, loopback, ambient
    comment: made with chirp-fixture
    extra: {"SUNO_ID": "11111111-2222-3333-4444-555555555555", "SUNO_HANDLE": "fixture"}
    no lyric field anywhere in the tags: fax
  -- when the API is unreachable, the page and the pattern answer --
  title from the meta tags: Loopback Lullaby
  audio from the pattern:   <base>/11111111-2222-3333-4444-555555555555.mp4  (mp4, 2249 bytes)
  via: guess  -- which is the sign the rungs above it need a look
  -- and the ones that must fail --
    a deleted song: SkillIssue -- there is no song with the id 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000 -- the link may have been deleted.
    not a link at all: SkillIssue -- that is not a Suno link, a song id, or a share code: 
    audio on a host we do not follow: SkillIssue -- this song's m4a is on 127.0.0.1, which is not a host this program follows. Pass --allow-host to add it.
